+## Capacity fixture clock
+
+The 20-second answer through a five-second reply buffer uses a paused
+current-thread Tokio clock for modeled playback and its scripted service.
+Every packet and capacity assertion remains; real IPC and authority freshness
+continue on the host clock. Shared helpers remain unpaused in the interruption
+case and the existing ignored long measurements.
+[Historical initial-base serial comparison](verification/capacity-clock-20261015/README.md):
+24.049 s to 0.516 s, with all 1,105 library identities and ignore flags retained
+on initial base `37b8be9e`. This timing pair and count are historical, not
+measurements of the current integration.
+The output labels fixture time explicitly. This is one test's clock migration;
+the original realtime group and its whole-group target remain unchanged.
